xtractingIdFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java-1989:1997,2029:2041-1989:1997,2029:2048","promptId":"#ZV025","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/TsidExtractingIdFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[{"pos":1989,"endPos":1997,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":64,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":72,"length":9},{"pos":2029,"endPos":2041,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":104,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":116,"length":13}],"dstChanges":[{"pos":1989,"endPos":1997,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":64,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":72,"length":9},{"pos":2029,"endPos":2048,"startLine":49,"startLineOffset":104,"endLine":49,"endLineOffset":123,"length":20}]}]}],"groundTruthGeneratedCommentsNodes":[{"groundTruth":{"original_line":956,"line":955,"comment_lines":["[][955]"],"review_comment":["This `isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled` check is unfortunate. The reason for it being here is that we can\u0027t fully trust `MapperBuilderContext#isDataStream`. In its current implementation `isDataStream` starts as `false` and then gets flipped to `true` if `DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper` is enabled in **current** mapping. This is broken for an edge case of a mapping overriding default `@timestamp` mapping (it is more generally broken for any mapping updates but this is the first time we experience that).\r\n\r\nScenario:\r\n1. Create a time series index with default mapping only\r\n2. Update mapping with\r\n```\r\n{\"@timestamp\": {\"type\": \"date\"}}\r\n```\r\nFor this mapping update `isDataStream` is `false` even though it was `true` previously.\r\n\r\nOne option to fix this is to pass existing mapping into `MappingParser#parse` and initialize `isDataStream` to a value based on it. I didn\u0027t want to mix this change in here.","Thanks for this explanation. Let\u0027s make fixing `MapperBuilderContext#isDataStream()` a followup of this change. As part of that change the ` \u0026\u0026 context.mappingLookup().isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled()` part of the condition can be removed."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","id":36737,"created_at":"2024-07-08T21:33:57Z","original_position":55,"side":"RIGHT","position":47,"submitted_on_commit":"f51dd2cd5350241e08accfe888e0c06d72861868","diff_hunk":"@@ -942,6 +947,30 @@ protected void parseCreateField(DocumentParserContext context) throws IOExceptio\n     }\n \n     private void indexValue(DocumentParserContext context, long timestamp) {\n+        // DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper and TsidExtractingFieldMapper need to use timestamp value,\n+        // so when this is true we store it in a well-known place\n+        // instead of forcing them to iterate over all fields.\n+        //\n+        // DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper is present and enabled both\n+        // in data streams and standalone indices in time_series mode\n+        if (isDataStreamTimestampField \u0026\u0026 context.mappingLookup().isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled()) {","submitted_line":956},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The logic in `indexValue` for handling data stream timestamp fields introduces new flags (`TIMESTAMP_VALUE_KEY` and `TIMESTAMP_MULTIPLE_VALUES_FLAG`). Ensure that these flags do not interfere with existing fields or cause issues if they are not set. Also, verify that the conditions for setting these flags are correct and cover all necessary cases.","nodes":[{"id":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java-server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java--38570:38662,38671:38728,38737:38791,38800:38802,38811:38872,38881:38942,38951:40010","promptId":"#QFEZC","srcPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","dstPath":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","srcChanges":[